WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.970
Before a scan, gel is spread on the skin,

2
00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.100
and the probe is pressed into it.

3
00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.740
Leave the gel out, and the
probe still sends ultrasound.

4
00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:11.380
But almost nothing useful comes back.

5
00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:13.900
Same probe, same frequency.

6
00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.580
One thin layer makes the difference.

7
00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:19.590
Why does the scan need that layer of gel?

8
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:22.800
In this mission, you'll
meet acoustic impedance:

9
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:26.270
a material's density times
the speed of sound in it.

10
00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:31.000
Then you'll use the frequency shift from
moving blood cells to find how fast blood

11
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.160
flows.

12
00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:36.980
The shift is in the range you can hear,
so scanners often play it as a sound.

13
00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:41.550
Your mission: explain why an ultrasound
scan needs a layer of gel between the

14
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:42.920
probe and the skin.
